Let $C$ be a $C^*$-algebra, let $m,n\ge1$ be integers, and let $d\in M_n(C)_+$ and $v\in M_m(C)_+$. Suppose $d\precsim v$ in $C\otimes\mathcal K$. For $\varepsilon>0$, put $h=(d-\varepsilon)_+$. There is $w\in M_{m,n}(C^{**})$ such that $$\label{eq:transport-supports}
 w^*w=e_h,\qquad ww^*\le e_v,$$ and $$\label{eq:transport-membership}
 w\operatorname{Her}_{M_n(C)}(h)\subset M_{m,n}(C),\qquad
 w\operatorname{Her}_{M_n(C)}(h)w^*\subset\operatorname{Her}_{M_m(C)}(v).$$ Conjugation by $w$ is an injective $*$-homomorphism on $\operatorname{Her}(h)$. For $l\in\operatorname{Her}(h)_+$, $$\label{eq:transport-cutoffs}
 (wlw^*-\tau)_+=w(l-\tau)_+w^*,\qquad
 w(l-\tau)_+w^*\sim_{\mathrm{Cu}}(l-\tau)_+\quad(\tau\ge0),$$ and $$\label{eq:transport-hereditary-image}
 w\operatorname{Her}(l)w^*=\operatorname{Her}(wlw^*).$$ Every representation, with matching matrix amplifications, satisfies $$\label{eq:transport-represented-norm}
 \|\pi^{(m)}(wkw^*)\|=\|\pi^{(n)}(k)\|
 \qquad(k\in\operatorname{Her}(h)).$$ The products in these formulas are algebra elements; $w$ itself is only asserted to lie in the bidual.

Let $C$ be a $C^*$-algebra, let $a,y\in C_+$ be contractions with $a$ rich, and let $c\in\widetilde C$ be a contraction. For an integer $k\ge1$ and fixed positive $\gamma_g,\sigma_g$ satisfying <a href="#eq:graph-constants" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:graph-constants">[eq:graph-constants]</a>, there are $$X\in\operatorname{Her}((a-1/8)_+)_+,\qquad
 B_1,\ldots,B_k\in\operatorname{Her}((a-1/8)_+)$$ with the following property. For any contractions $$S_i\in\operatorname{Her}((X-\alpha_0)_+),\qquad 1\le i\le k,$$ one can form a rich positive contraction $p\in\operatorname{Her}(a)$ such that, for every representation $\pi$ of $C$, $\|\pi(a)\|>1/2$ implies $\|\pi(p)\|=1$. If a representation $\pi$ of $C$ satisfies $$\pi\bigl(y(1-c^*p^2c)y\bigr)=0,\qquad \|\pi(y)\|>s,$$ then, in that same representation, $$\label{eq:graph-failure}
 \|\pi(X)\|>s,\qquad \pi(B_i)=\pi(S_i)\quad(1\le i\le k).$$ The elements $X,B_1,\ldots,B_k$ are fixed before the $S_i$ are chosen.

Let $C$ be a $C^*$-algebra, let $a,y\in C_+$ be contractions with $a$ rich, and let $c\in\widetilde C$ be a contraction. Suppose $p\in\operatorname{Her}(a)$ is a rich positive contraction satisfying $$\|\pi(a)\|>1/2\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|\pi(p)\|=1
 \qquad\text{for every representation }\pi\text{ of }C.$$ Put $d=y(1-c^*p^2c)y\in C_+$, and assume $$\label{eq:common-nonvanishing}
 \pi(d)=0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|\pi(y)\|\le\frac14
 \qquad\text{for every representation }\pi\text{ of }C.$$ Then there are positive contractions $$p_1\in\operatorname{Her}(a),\qquad q_1\in\operatorname{Her}(y)$$ such that $p_1$ is rich, $$\label{eq:shrinking-signals}
 \begin{split}
  \|\pi(a)\|>1/2&\ \Longrightarrow\ \|\pi(p_1)\|=1,\\
  \|\pi(y)\|>1/2&\ \Longrightarrow\ \|\pi(q_1)\|=1
 \end{split}
 \qquad\text{for every representation }\pi\text{ of }C,$$ and $$\label{eq:shrinking-support}
 \|e_{p_1}c e_{q_1}\|_{C^{**}}<1.$$ The last inequality is a single norm bound in the universal bidual.

Suppose $C$ satisfies $\textup{(P)}$. Let $X\in C_+$ and $B_1,B_2,B_3,B_4\in C$. With $$\alpha_0=\frac1{32}<\alpha=\frac1{16}
 <\beta=\frac18<s=\frac14,\qquad h=\frac12,$$ there exist contractions $T_1,\ldots,T_4$ in $\operatorname{Her}((X-\alpha_0)_+)$ for which no representation $\pi$ of $C$ satisfies $$\label{eq:four-forbidden}
 \|\pi(X)\|>s,\qquad \pi(B_i)=\pi(T_i)\quad(1\le i\le4).$$

Suppose $C$ satisfies $\textup{(P)}$. Let $a,y\in C$ be positive contractions and let $c\in\widetilde C$ be a contraction. There are positive contractions $p_1\in\operatorname{Her}(a)$ and $q_1\in\operatorname{Her}(y)$, with $p_1$ rich, such that for every representation $\pi$ of $C$, $$\label{eq:shrinking-P-signals}
 \|\pi(a)\|>1/2\ \Longrightarrow\ \|\pi(p_1)\|=1,
 \qquad
 \|\pi(y)\|>1/2\ \Longrightarrow\ \|\pi(q_1)\|=1,$$ and, in the universal bidual, $$\label{eq:shrinking-P-support}
 \|e_{p_1}c e_{q_1}\|<1.$$

Let $(C_i)_{i\in I}$ be any family of $C^*$-algebras satisfying $\textup{(P)}$. Their bounded product $D=\prod_{i\in I}C_i$ satisfies $\textup{(P)}$. More precisely, for a positive contraction $d=(d_i)\in D$ and $0<\delta<1/2$, there is a row $s=(s_i)\in M_{1,2}(D)$ such that $$\label{eq:product-row}
 s^*ds=(d-2\delta)_+\oplus(d-2\delta)_+,\qquad
 \|s\|\le\delta^{-1/2}.$$

There are $\ell\ge1$, a $C^*$-algebra $W$, contractions $z_1,\ldots,z_\ell\in W$, and contractions $z_j^{(r)}\in M_{N_r}(\mathbb C)$, where $N_r\ge1$, $r\ge1$, and $1\le j\le\ell$, with the following properties.*

1.  *No tuple $b_1,\ldots,b_\ell$ in any exact $C^*$-algebra satisfies $$\label{eq:forbidden-tuple}
     \left\|\sum_{j=1}^{\ell} A_j\otimes b_j\right\|
     =\left\|\sum_{j=1}^{\ell} A_j\otimes z_j\right\|
     \quad\text{for every }m\ge1\text{ and every }A_j\in M_m(\mathbb C).$$*


2.  *For every fixed $m\ge1$ and $A_j\in M_m(\mathbb C)$, $$\label{eq:tuple-approximations}
     \lim_{r\to\infty}
     \left\|\sum_{j=1}^{\ell} A_j\otimes z_j^{(r)}\right\|
     =\left\|\sum_{j=1}^{\ell} A_j\otimes z_j\right\|.$$

Let $C$ be nuclear and satisfy $\textup{(F\ensuremath{_n})}$ for one fixed $n\ge1$. Let $a,y\in C_+$ be contractions, with $a$ rich, and let $c\in\widetilde C$ be a contraction. There are positive contractions $p_1\in\operatorname{Her}(a)$ and $q_1\in\operatorname{Her}(y)$ such that $p_1$ is rich, $$\label{eq:nuclear-shrinking-signals}
 \begin{split}
 \|\pi(a)\|>1/2&\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|\pi(p_1)\|=1,\\
 \|\pi(y)\|>1/2&\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|\pi(q_1)\|=1
 \end{split}
 \qquad\text{for every representation }\pi,$$ and $\|e_{p_1}ce_{q_1}\|_{C^{**}}<1$.

Let $C$ be nuclear and satisfy $\textup{(F\ensuremath{_n})}$ for a fixed $n\ge1$. For $u\in C_+$ and rich positive contractions $a,b\in\operatorname{Her}(u)$, there is a rich positive contraction $c_0\in\operatorname{Her}(u)$ such that every representation $\pi$ satisfies $$\label{eq:merger-signal}
 \bigl(\|\pi(a)\|>1/2\ \text{or}\ \|\pi(b)\|>1/2\bigr)
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|\pi(c_0)\|=1.$$

For every integer $r\geq1$ and every $Z\in M_r(\mathcal U)$ whose entries are $*$-polynomials in $u,u^*$, $$\label{eq:finite-matrix-tests}
 \|Z\|_{M_r(\mathcal U)}
 =\sup_{d\geq1,\ D\in M_d(\mathbb C),\ \|D\|\leq1}\|Z(D,D^*)\|.$$

Let $E\subset\mathcal U$ be a finite-dimensional linear space consisting of $*$-polynomials in $u,u^*$. There is a finite constant $C_E\geq0$ with the following property. Suppose $v$ is a contraction in a unital $C^*$-algebra $B$, and fix one number $\theta>0$. Assume that for every integer $d\geq1$ and every contraction $D\in M_d(\mathbb C)$, there are a unital representation $\pi:B\to B(H_\pi)$ and an isometry $J:\mathbb C^d\to H_\pi$ satisfying the two inequalities in <a href="#eq:forbidden-models" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:forbidden-models">[eq:forbidden-models]</a> with $\theta$ in place of $\gamma$. For the homomorphism $\Phi:\mathcal U\to B$ with $\Phi(u)=v$, one then has $$\label{eq:all-amplification-bound}
 \|\Phi^{(r)}(Z)\|\geq(1-C_E\theta)\|Z\|
 \qquad (r\geq1,\ Z\in M_r(E)).$$

Let $C$ be a $C^*$-algebra, let $Q,c\in C_+$ with $\|c\|\le1$, and let $m>0$. If $c\precsim(Q^2-m^2/4)_+$, then for each $0<\delta<1$ there is $x\in C$ such that $$\label{eq:separation-bounded-implementation}
 \|(Qx)^*(Qx)-c\|<\delta,\qquad
 \|Qx\|\le2,\qquad \|x\|\le\frac4m.$$
